# Kaggle public episodes, 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-27

Owner request 2026-09-28: refresh the RunPod network volume with the latest 14 days of the
official daily top-episodes dataset (forum topic 731215,
`kaggle/kaggriculture-episodes-index`).

## Location

- Volume: `kggriv2-shared-1tb` (`4llk4uaf20`, EU-RO-1), mounted at `/workspace`
  (pod `p0wdnd40cbmrej`).
- Root: `/workspace/kaggriculture-v2/public-episodes-2026-09-14-to-2026-09-27/`
  - `archives/kaggriculture-episodes-YYYY-MM-DD.zip`: one ZIP per day, flat
    `<episode_id>.json` members plus `manifest.csv`. Not extracted
    (about 300 GB of JSON uncompressed).
  - `daily-manifests/YYYY-MM-DD.json`: per-day archive SHA-256, per-episode sizes, origin.
  - `manifest.json`: whole-range summary and verification flags.
  - `index-manifest-2026-09-28.csv`: the official index used for verification
    (SHA-256 `caaf1339…6da79`, also committed here).
- The earlier `public-episodes-2026-09-06-to-2026-09-19/` root is left in place. Days
  09-14..09-19 in the new root are hard links to its verified archives (no extra space).

## Verification

`download_recent.py` checks every archive: ZIP CRC over all members, only `.json` plus one
`manifest.csv`, and episode count and total uncompressed JSON bytes equal to the official
index row for that day. The 2026-09-20 root's recorded counts and bytes for 09-12..09-19
matched the index exactly before this run.

## 2026-09-26 rebuild

Kaggle's whole-dataset ZIP for 2026-09-26 returned HTTP 404 on 2026-09-28 ("Awaiting
Compression", as reported in the forum topic), although its 597 files were listed.
`rebuild_day_from_files.py` fetched each listed file from the per-file endpoint, checked
each size against `files-2026-09-26.csv`, and wrote a deflated ZIP with the same flat
layout. Its SHA-256 is of this local container, not an official Kaggle archive; its
contents pass the same index count/byte checks as the other days.

## Run

```
python3 download_recent.py --root <root> --start 2026-09-14 --end 2026-09-27 \
  --index-manifest <root>/index-manifest-2026-09-28.csv \
  --reuse-root /workspace/kaggriculture-v2/public-episodes-2026-09-06-to-2026-09-19 --workers 4
python3 rebuild_day_from_files.py --root <root> --day 2026-09-26 \
  --file-list <root>/files-2026-09-26.csv --workers 8
```

## Result

Completed 2026-09-28 09:04 UTC (`manifest.json`, `download.log`):
14 datasets, 8,766 episodes, 9,345,988,457 archive bytes (8.8 GB on the volume, 6 days
shared by hard link), 300,362,654,536 uncompressed JSON bytes. All ZIP CRC, inventory and
index count/byte checks pass.

- 09-14..09-19: hard links from the 2026-09-20 root; archive SHA-256 and per-episode sizes
  equal that root's daily manifests.
- 09-20..09-25, 09-27: official Kaggle archives, downloaded 08:55–08:56 UTC.
- 09-26: rebuilt from 597 per-file downloads (`rebuild-2026-09-26.log`), 538,684,154 bytes.

The first pass (`download-attempt1.log`) records each day's origin; it exited on the 09-26
404. The second pass revalidated all 14 archives in place, so `manifest.json` records
`origin: present` for every day.

